Welcome to the Masruroh Inventory System repository. This guide provides step-by-step instructions on how to clone and run the project on your local machine. 

Prerequisites
Ensure the following software is installed on your system:
PHP (Version 8.2 or later)
Composer
Node.js & NPM
MySQL (or MariaDB/XAMPP/Laragon)
Git

Installation Steps
Follow the steps below to set up and run the project:
1. Clone the Repository
Open your terminal (Command Prompt/PowerShell/Git Bash) and run:
#git clone https://github.com/your-username/your-repository.git
#cd your-repository

(Replace the URL above with your actual GitHub repository URL.)

2. Install Dependencies
Install the required PHP and JavaScript dependencies:
#composer install
#npm install

3. Configure the Environment (.env)
Copy the example environment file .env.example to .env:
#cp .env.example .env
(On Windows Command Prompt use: copy .env.example .env)

Open the .env file and update your database configuration:
DB_CONNECTION=mysql
DB_HOST=127.0.0.1
DB_PORT=3306
DB_DATABASE=inventory_db  # Replace with your database name
DB_USERNAME=root          # Adjust your database username
DB_PASSWORD=              # Adjust your database password

4. Generate Application Key
Generate the Laravel application encryption key:
#php artisan key:generate

5. Set Up the Database
Create a new database in MySQL (e.g., inventory_db) if it does not exist. Then run the migrations and seeders:
#php artisan migrate --seed
This command will create all necessary tables and insert initial data (such as the default admin account).

6. Build Frontend Assets
Compile CSS and JavaScript assets:
#npm run build

7. Run the Application
Start the Laravel local development server:
#php artisan serve

Access the application in your browser at:
http://localhost:8000

Default Login Credentials (If Seeder Is Used)
If using the default seeder, you may log in with:
Email: admin@example.com (or as defined in the seeder)

Password: password (or as defined in the seeder)
